WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.700
The UN Charter was signed

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.404
in San Francisco in 1945.

3
00:00:05.404 --> 00:00:07.404
Its Security Council still has

4
00:00:07.404 --> 00:00:10.024
the same five permanent members.

5
00:00:10.365 --> 00:00:12.548
The Charter was signed on

6
00:00:12.548 --> 00:00:14.731
the twenty-sixth of June,

7
00:00:14.731 --> 00:00:16.674
1945. It came into force

8
00:00:16.674 --> 00:00:18.701
on the twenty-fourth of October:

9
00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:19.731
UN Day.

10
00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:21.807
The UN has six principal

11
00:00:21.807 --> 00:00:24.757
organs, including the General Assembly,

12
00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:26.507
the Security Council and the

13
00:00:26.507 --> 00:00:28.903
International Court of Justice.

14
00:00:29.241 --> 00:00:31.132
The five permanent members have

15
00:00:31.132 --> 00:00:31.910
a veto.

16
00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:34.587
That's why reform keeps stalling.

17
00:00:34.933 --> 00:00:36.110
Your turn.

18
00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:38.109
When is UN Day?
